    {
      "id": "2115640651517939785",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2103567689515954176/aR-Kjpp4_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-10-29T03:03:32.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-29 11:03:32",
      "type": "引用",
      "type_label": "引用",
      "text": "If you look closely enough, breakthroughs in everything are accelerating exponentially. \n\nAn exponential always starts off looking small.",
      "quote": {
        "author": "m_goes_distance",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1919598657047035904/BYOefMqX_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-28 00:01:19",
        "created_at_utc": "2026-10-27T16:01:19.000Z",
        "id": "2115111611652276717",
        "images": [],
        "media": [],
        "name": "Mgoes (bio/acc 🤖💉)",
        "text": "this might be my last normal tweet before biotech goes vertical\n\ni'm not a whistleblower. I don't work at Lilly, Novo or any of the big labs\n\nbut there is a massive shift happening in human biology right now. \n\nit's sitting in press releases and almost nobody reads them\n\nthe last 6 months alone:\n\n- a once-daily pill roughly doubled median survival in metastatic pancreatic cancer (13.2 vs 6.6 months)\n- a one-time gene editing infusion cut hereditary angioedema attacks 87%, and 62% of patients stayed attack-free and off all other prevention for 6 months\n- a one-time gene edit for cholesterol dropped LDL up to 62%, and it held for over a year\n- a personalized mrna vaccine beat keytruda alone in a 1,137 patient melanoma phase 3\n- retatrutide hit ~28% weight loss in a phase 3\n- an ai-designed drug entered phase 3\n- a pill that regrows hair passed its second phase 3\n- an immunotherapy that could let some rectal cancer patients skip surgery, chemo and radiation just got fda approved\n- a man lived 271 days off dialysis on a pig kidney\n- human cells were caught passing chromosome-sized chunks of DNA to their neighbors, and it changes how the neighbors behave\n\nwe are on the verge of an era where the human body is a software problem and the update cycle gets shorter everyday\n\nstick around, it's going to get weird\n\nbio/acc",
        "url": "https://x.com/m_goes_distance/status/2115111611652276717",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
      "reply_to": "",
